course: dictionary
lesson: 11831
title: Blackening: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word blackening comes from black. It can mean becoming black or darker, or making something black. «The sky was blackening as the storm rolled in.» The sky was getting darker, so blackening means turning dark.
explain: Blackening can also mean damaging someone's good name by saying bad things about them. «The rumours were blackening her name at school.» Nothing is burnt or painted here. The sentence is about what people say, so the context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Ask yourself: is something turning dark, or is someone being hurt by words? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Blackening is the -ing form of the verb blacken.
fact: «Blackening» can mean becoming black or darker, as in «the toast was blackening in the oven».
fact: «Blackening» can mean damaging someone's good name by saying bad things about them.
fact: As a noun, blackening is the process or result of something going black, like rotting fruit.
fact: In cooking, blackening is a way of cooking fish or meat with spices in a very hot pan.
exercise: «The sky was blackening, and thunder rumbled over the hills.» What is happening to the sky? | *Getting darker | Filling with stars | Getting lighter | Turning green
exercise: «The gossip was blackening her name at school.» What does blackening mean here? | Writing her name in black ink | *Damaging her good name with bad stories | Making her name famous | Painting her name on the wall
exercise: Mum says the bananas are blackening on the kitchen side. What is happening to them? | Growing taller | Getting cold | *Going black as they rot | Being washed in cold water
test: «He spent the evening blackening the fish in a very hot pan with spices.» What does blackening mean in this sentence? | Painting the fish black | Washing the fish in cold water | *Cooking with spices in a very hot pan | Hiding the fish from the cat
test: Which sentence uses blackening as a noun, meaning the process of something going black? | Blackening is a fun game we play at break | *The blackening of the old wall took many years | She is blackening the pan with a spoon
exam: «The rumour was blackening his name, but the truth came out.» What does blackening mean here? | Writing his name in neat letters | Making his name shorter | Covering his name in paint | *Ruining his good name with lies
